From 51d4cde07c65cf9b384b2bed2c72dfe8fd61931f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ben Wong <BenWongCityuCS@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 22:20:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ui): bound renderer conversation window on real-user
 queries

Long conversations grow rows.window without bound (row.appended appends,
nothing evicts), and the turn-navigator's wide-screen auto loadAllOlder
pulls the entire history back in - renderer memory grows with session
length and the UI lags noticeably on very long turns (reproduced on a
desktop i5-12400/64GB, ZCode Desktop 3.14.x).

This bounds the CLIENT display window only; the protocol layer
(apply.ts) and the server projection (rowsRange pagination source) are
untouched, so full history stays reachable via loadOlder.

- conversationWindowBound.ts (new, pure functions + unit tests):
  * boundWindowOnRealUserQuery: on a real-user query append, keep the
    turns of the last 10 real queries in the window (turn-tagged rows
    stay together; synthetic rows do not trigger trimming; identity
    stable when nothing is trimmed). Rows leave the window, not the
    log: canLoadOlder keeps holding and scroll-to-top loadOlder pages
    them back.
  * mergeSnapshotTailOntoLocalWindow: snapshots only carry the tail
    (snapshotTailWindowRows); a mid-long-turn resync used to replace the
    wholesale window with that tail, wiping earlier queries. When the
    incoming snapshot is the same logEpoch and a strict append
    extension, the local prefix rows are kept in front of the tail
    (guarded by monotonic totalCount/rowId and the snapshot's own
    earlier-row budget); otherwise the wholesale replace still applies.
- conversationProjectionStore.ts: apply both at the two frame paths.
- conversationTurnNavigatorHelpers.ts: navigator ticks are derived from
  rows.window, so the auto full-history hydration defeats any window
  bound; it is now gated off (ticks degrade to bookmarks of the loaded
  window and grow as loadOlder expands history; share-view hydration is
  a separate path and is unaffected). A future lightweight query
  directory could restore full tick lists without loading all rows.

Tests: node --test (or tsx) on packages/ui/test/conversationWindowBound.test.ts
